WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.700
Next up, did you ever have your phone buzz

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.640
only to look down and read a text that says, "Can we talk?"

3
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:10.920
Oh my God.

4
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.230
Refinery29 reports that experts say

5
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.600
you should never text that to anyone.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.000
If you text, "We need to talk,"

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.260 line:15%
it immediately makes people think about

8
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.670 line:15%
the absolute worst case scenarios.

9
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.500 line:15%
It's a heart attack in a text message

10
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.840 line:15%
and should never be done.

11
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.350 line:15%
Rossy, thoughts.

12
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.770 line:15%
Don't you dare text me this, okay?

13
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:32.650 line:15%
Just come out and say it

14
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.270 line:15%
because you know what I've done in that 18 seconds

15
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.380 line:15%
between "Hey, we need to talk," and the bubble?

16
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.880 line:15%
Is that I've decided everyone died, right?

17
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.270
Everyone's gone. They're just dead.

18
00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.840
There's a bomb on the way. Hey, you know, boom.

19
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.750
So every single worst case scenario.

20
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.640
You know, they canceled "Bridgerton."

21
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:52.473
What? No!

22
00:00:52.473 --> 00:00:54.960
What? Something terrible is coming.

23
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.080
Just give it to me straight.
(Drew laughs)

24
00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.510
I feel like I've gotten a lot of them

25
00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.090
in the last few years.

26
00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.140
Like, they're constantly like an onslaught

27
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.660
of the "Can we talk" texts.

28
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.640
What would be a good alternative? Does anyone have an idea?

29
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.090
Yes, you!

30
00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.090
What is your name?

31
00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.923
I'm Jo.

32
00:01:14.923 --> 00:01:16.350
Hi, Jo. I'm Drew, this is Ross.

33
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.272
Hi, Jo!

34
00:01:17.272 --> 00:01:18.900
Hi!

35
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.530
I take it from a science point of view.

36
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.670
You state the problem

37
00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:25.420
and come up with possible hypotheses and solutions.

38
00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.280
Right away.
All in the same text?

39
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.250
All in the same text.

40
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.307
So you say, "Hey, here's a problem,

41
00:01:29.307 --> 00:01:30.487
"this is what it is,

42
00:01:30.487 --> 00:01:31.627
"this is what I think we should do about it,

43
00:01:31.627 --> 00:01:32.730
"have a great day"?

44
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.080
Yes.
(audience laughs)

45
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.590
I agree.

46
00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:40.460
I think stating the problem right there in text,

47
00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.300
and then the possible solutions,

48
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.140
or at least a, "Now let's get into it."

49
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:46.973
Exactly.

50
00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.490
What do you do for living, may I ask?

51
00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:50.770
I'm a science teacher.

52
00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.135
Yeah.
Oh, that explains it.

53
00:01:52.135 --> 00:01:53.090
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

54
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.472
There you go.

55
00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:57.583
Cause and effect. Problem, solution.

56
00:01:59.055 --> 00:02:00.230
Thank you, Jo.

57
00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.620
I really think you did solve the problem

58
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.380
and I appreciate you endlessly.

59
00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.213
Thank you, Jo.

60
00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:06.633
Leave it to a science teacher.

61
00:02:06.633 --> 00:02:08.070
(audience applauds)

62
00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.640
All right, thanks Jo.

63
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.610
All right, next up it's Taco Time in today's Food News!

64
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.724
Num, num, num, num!
Num, num, num, num!

65
